// BMP - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A real BMP: the file header starts BM, the DIB header is 40 bytes for a
# BITMAPINFOHEADER, and the pixel data follows bottom-up. Here the pixels
# spell "Hello World!" as 24-bit BGR.
0000  42 4D 66 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 36 00 00 00 28 00 |BMf.......6...(.|
0010  00 00 01 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 01 00 18 00 00 00 |................|
0020  00 00 0C 00 00 00 13 0B 00 00 13 0B 00 00 00 00 |................|
0030  00 00 00 00 00 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C |......Hello Worl|
0040  64 21                                           |d!|
